# WORKLOAD_MANIFEST — canonical production scheduled-workload intended state
# (GH-104 Phase B).
#
# This is the ONE authoritative intended-state declaration for every
# production-relevant systemd service/timer/path under deploy/systemd/.
# MANAGED_UNITS remains the literal allowlist scripts/deploy_server.sh
# reads to install/enable units — it is a mechanical VIEW derived from
# this manifest (every row below with auto_install=true), not a second,
# independently-maintained source of truth. backend/tests/
# test_gh104_scheduled_workload_reconciliation.py asserts the two files
# cannot silently drift apart.
#
# Columns (pipe-delimited, no spaces around `|`):
#
#   unit           — exact filename under deploy/systemd/, OR a synthetic
#                    identifier in angle brackets for a workload that is
#                    intentionally NOT YET represented by a repo file (see
#                    repo_status=absent below). Never a real path outside
#                    deploy/systemd/.
#   classification — one of:
#     required        must be running in production; standard deploy
#                      installs/updates it, and enables --now the
#                      timer/path member of the pair.
#     deferred         repo keeps the unit; production intentionally does
#                      NOT auto-install/auto-enable it pending explicit
#                      policy/PM approval. Its absence must never fail a
#                      required-unit assertion.
#     manual-oneshot   no [Install] section by design; started by hand
#                      only, never via a timer/path, never auto-enabled.
#     deprecated       must not re-enter the managed install/enable set;
#                      if a repo file exists it is documentation-only.
#     static-helper    exists on disk for other units to invoke on demand
#                      (systemd template instantiation or OnFailure=);
#                      itself is never `enable`d/`start`ed by name.
#     template         a `@`-instantiated unit template; not itself
#                      installed/enabled — a future concrete instance
#                      would be added as its own row.
#     out-of-scope     intentionally outside this manifest's ownership
#                      (a different lifecycle/deployment owns it); listed
#                      here only so its absence is never mistaken for an
#                      oversight.
#   repo_status    — present (file exists under deploy/systemd/) or
#                    absent (classification=required workload with NO
#                    repo file yet — a known, explicitly tracked
#                    reproducibility gap; see the notes column and
#                    docs/operations/scheduled-workload-manifest.md).
#   auto_install   — true if scripts/deploy_server.sh step 10 installs/
#                    updates this file every deploy (i.e. it is listed in
#                    MANAGED_UNITS). Always false when repo_status=absent
#                    (nothing to install) or classification is anything
#                    other than required/static-helper.
#   auto_enable    — true if step 10 also runs `enable --now` on it.
#                    Only ever true for a .timer/.path row; a .service
#                    row is installed (so its trigger can find it) but
#                    never enabled directly — see MANAGED_UNITS' own
#                    header for why.
#   trigger_type   — timer | path | oneshot-on-demand | template | n/a
#   destructive    — true if unintended activation deletes/mutates
#                    customer data irreversibly. A destructive row that
#                    is somehow found enabled in production must FAIL a
#                    post-deploy assertion, not just WARN.
#   notes          — human-readable reason/context.

wecom-archive-worker.service|required|present|true|false|oneshot|false|Callback-primary archive sync/decrypt worker; the timer below is the reconciliation fallback, not the primary trigger.
wecom-archive-worker.timer|required|present|true|true|timer|false|5-minute fallback reconciliation (OnCalendar=*:0/5) behind the callback-primary path.
wecom-external-contact-reconcile.service|required|present|true|false|oneshot|false|Daily full external-contact metadata + avatar-sync reconciliation; backstops the incremental refresh path below.
wecom-external-contact-reconcile.timer|required|present|true|true|timer|false|Daily 04:15 full reconciliation.
wecom-external-contact-refresh.service|required|present|true|false|oneshot|false|Bounded (EXTERNAL_CONTACT_REFRESH_BATCH_SIZE, default 25), tenant-scoped, retry/backoff-safe incremental refresh queue drain.
wecom-external-contact-refresh.path|required|present|true|true|path|false|PRIMARY low-latency trigger: producer touches a coalescing mtime-only signal after enqueueing a refresh task; carries no task payload.
wecom-external-contact-refresh.timer|required|present|true|true|timer|false|FALLBACK/recovery trigger only (OnBootSec=10min, OnUnitInactiveSec=15min) — recovers retryable tasks after a restart or a missed/failed path wake-up. The .path above is primary; this timer must never be treated as the low-latency path.
wecom-archive-media-download.service|required|present|true|false|oneshot|false|Generic pending/retryable media reconciliation (RND-343 canonical design); reused verbatim by the event path below — not a second downloader.
wecom-archive-media-download.timer|required|present|true|true|timer|false|FALLBACK/recovery cadence only: every 30 minutes (OnCalendar=*:15/30). This is the PM-approved canonical cadence — do not regress to the old 5-minute polling semantics observed on production pre-GH-104.
wecom-archive-media-event.service|required|present|true|false|oneshot|false|Archive-complete event handler; invokes the identical generic media worker CLI as the timer above, so the two triggers can never create duplicate media records or divergent behavior.
wecom-archive-media-event.path|required|present|true|true|path|false|PRIMARY low-latency trigger: archive worker signals this coalescing mtime-only path only when a successful commit left pending media. The 30-minute timer above is the fallback for a missed signal, not a competing primary.
wecom-export-jobs.service|required|present|true|false|oneshot|false|Generates queued export ZIPs, retries notification email, deletes seven-day-expired artifacts. Requires the effective worker environment to resolve MEDIA_STORAGE_PROVIDER=qiniu_kodo from backend/.env alone — see docs/operations/scheduled-workload-manifest.md's export-jobs section for the systemd drop-in that must NOT exist.
wecom-export-jobs.timer|required|present|true|true|timer|false|Every 5 minutes (OnCalendar=*:04/5).
wecom-ai-kb-eval.service|required|present|true|false|oneshot|false|Daily retrieval-quality launch gate against the fixed eval set; records ai_eval_runs.
wecom-ai-kb-eval.timer|required|present|true|true|timer|false|Daily 05:00.
wecom-ai-kb-gap-report.service|required|present|true|false|oneshot|false|Weekly Markdown candidate-improvement report under docs/ai/reports/; never creates, changes, or closes GitHub Issues.
wecom-ai-kb-gap-report.timer|required|present|true|true|timer|false|Weekly Monday 06:00.
wecom-ai-kb-reindex.service|required|present|true|false|oneshot|false|Rebuilds the AI support knowledge-base retrieval index from backend/app/ai_kb/manifest.json; no-op if AI_SUPPORT_ENABLED is unset.
wecom-ai-kb-reindex.timer|required|present|true|true|timer|false|Hourly at :15.
wecom-ai-retention-sweep.service|required|present|true|false|oneshot|false|Deletes AI chat sessions/messages past AI_RETENTION_DAYS (default 90). Distinct from the deferred public-retention sweep below.
wecom-ai-retention-sweep.timer|required|present|true|true|timer|false|Daily 03:30.
wecom-billing-lifecycle.service|required|present|true|false|oneshot|false|GH-106 commercial-loop lifecycle projector; row-locked, idempotent, failure-isolated; scans only tenants that already have a Subscription.
wecom-billing-lifecycle.timer|required|present|true|true|timer|false|Every 5 minutes (OnCalendar=*:07/5).
wecom-billing-notifications.service|required|present|true|false|oneshot|false|GH-106 lifecycle/payment-activation/refund-anomaly notification dispatch.
wecom-billing-notifications.timer|required|present|true|true|timer|false|Every 5 minutes (OnCalendar=*:02/5).
wecom-payment-recovery.service|required|present|true|false|oneshot|false|GH-106 bounded WeChat order recovery; queries existing orders only, never creates checkout.
